    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Gotcha. One thing though, I've heard stories from some guys on the job site about decks having weird, sudden issues—like things just snapping or shifting unexpectedly even when the math seems okay. Is that usually just bad luck with the timber, or is there something else that can cause those kinds of random structural failures?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
