      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those sudden failures are rarely just bad luck; they often stem from installation errors like inadequate foundation grip, under-tightened fasteners, or poor connection details that compromise structural integrity. Additionally, Cedar may have hidden internal decay or grain warping that isn't visible during inspection, which can cause members to snap unexpectedly under stress. To prevent this, ensure all connections are rigorously tightened to code and that your foundation posts use continuous helical ties or chemical anchors rated for Vancouver's freeze-thaw cycles. Even with perfect math, a weak connection point is the most common cause of premature disaster.",
